# WGS CNV Pipeline

A Nextflow DSL2 pipeline for generating Log R Ratio (LRR) and B Allele Frequency (BAF) signals from whole-genome sequencing (WGS) gVCF files, enabling copy number variant (CNV) detection with PennCNV.

> **Publication in preparation.** Please contact the authors before using this pipeline in your own research.

---

## Overview

This pipeline takes individual-level gVCF files and population-level pVCF files as input, computes per-sample LRR/BAF signal intensities at SNP positions, and outputs PFB-normalized BAF/LRR files ready for PennCNV-based CNV calling.

```
pVCF (chr1–22)  ──► PLINK merge & QC ──► Select unrelated samples
gVCF (per sample) ──► BAF/LRR extraction ──► PFB estimation ──► Filtered BAF/LRR
```

### Key features

- Fully parallelized on SLURM HPC clusters (tested on Compute Canada / Rorqual)
- Processes thousands of samples efficiently via batched SLURM jobs
- Supports DeepVariant-style gVCF format (GRCh38)
- Automatic retry on memory/time limit failures

---

## Requirements

### Software

| Tool | Version tested | Purpose |
|------|---------------|---------|
| [Nextflow](https://www.nextflow.io/) | ≥ 23.10 | Workflow manager |
| [PLINK2](https://www.cog-genomics.org/plink/2.0/) | 2.0 | Genotype filtering and merging |
| [bcftools](https://samtools.github.io/bcftools/) | ≥ 1.17 | VCF processing |
| [Perl](https://www.perl.org/) | ≥ 5.30 | `fromgVCFToSignalIntensity.pl` |
| [GNU parallel](https://www.gnu.org/software/parallel/) | ≥ 20230522 | Parallel sample processing |
| [Python](https://www.python.org/) | ≥ 3.10 | PFB computation |
| [Polars](https://pola.rs/) | ≥ 1.0, < 1.23 | Dataframe operations |

### Input files

- **pVCF files**: one per chromosome (chr1–22), e.g. `cohort.deepvariant.chr1.vcf.gz`
- **gVCF files**: one per sample, e.g. `SP0001234.gvcf.gz` — standard gVCF format including both variant and non-variant positions (compatible with DeepVariant, All of Us, and similar pipelines)
- **Genome resources**: GRCh38 problematic regions BED file (included in `scripts/resources/`)

---

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/JacquemontLab/WGS_pipeline.git
cd WGS_pipeline
```

---

## Configuration

Edit `nextflow.config` to set your input/output paths and cluster parameters:

```groovy
params {
    inputDirpVCF      = "/path/to/pvcf_directory"      // pVCF files (chr1–22)
    inputDirgVCF      = "/path/to/gvcf_directory"      // individual gVCF files
    outputDir         = "/path/to/output_directory"
    scriptDir         = "/path/to/WGS_pipeline/scripts"

    topN              = 1000      // number of unrelated samples for PFB estimation
    gvcf_batch_size   = 125       // samples per SLURM job (gVCF → BAF/LRR step)
    filter_batch_size = 250       // samples per SLURM job (filtering step)
    n_batches         = 20        // number of batches for PFB partial computation
    polars_threads    = 4         // threads per pfb_partial job

    PLINK_filter_options = "--geno 0.05 --mind 0.05 --hwe 1e-6 --maf 0.001"
}
```

### SLURM configuration

The default configuration targets Compute Canada clusters with the `rrg-jacquese` account. Adjust `clusterOptions` for your cluster:

```groovy
process {
    clusterOptions = '--account=YOUR_ACCOUNT'
}
```

---

## Usage

### On a SLURM cluster

```bash
sbatch --account=YOUR_ACCOUNT --time=24:00:00 --mem=4G --cpus-per-task=2 \
  --wrap="module load nextflow && nextflow run main.nf -with-report"
```

### Resume a previous run

```bash
nextflow run main.nf -resume -with-report
```

### Override parameters at runtime

```bash
nextflow run main.nf \
  --inputDirgVCF /path/to/gvcf \
  --topN 500 \
  --gvcf_batch_size 100 \
  -resume
```

---

## Pipeline steps

| Step | Process | Description |
|------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | `pVCF_to_plink` | Convert pVCF (chr1–22, autosomes only) to PLINK binary format |
| 2 | `plink_filter_merge` | Apply QC filters and merge chromosomes into a single dataset |
| 3 | `select_unrel_topN` | Select top N unrelated samples (lowest missingness) for PFB estimation |
| 4 | `gvcf_to_signalintensity` | Extract BAF/LRR signals from individual gVCF files (~125 samples/job) |
| 5 | `split_iids` | Split selected sample IDs into batches for parallel PFB computation |
| 6 | `pfb_partial` | Compute partial PFB statistics per batch of samples |
| 7 | `pfb_reduce` | Aggregate partial PFBs into a final `PFB.tsv` file |
| 8 | `filter_baf_lrr_files` | Filter BAF/LRR files using the final PFB (~250 samples/job) |

---

## Output

```
results/
├── merged_dataset.bed / .bim / .fam     # merged PLINK dataset (autosomes)
├── stats/
│   ├── merged_dataset.missing.smiss    # per-sample missingness
│   └── merged_dataset.missing.vmiss    # per-variant missingness
├── keep_unrel_topN.iid.txt             # selected unrelated sample IDs
├── LRR_BAF/
│   └── <SAMPLE_ID>.baf_lrr.tsv        # raw BAF/LRR per sample
├── PFB.tsv                             # population frequency of B allele
└── LRR_BAF_filtered/
    └── <SAMPLE_ID>_filtered.baf_lrr.tsv  # PFB-normalized BAF/LRR (PennCNV input)
```

---


## Resource requirements (approximate)

| Step | CPUs | Memory | Wall time |
|------|------|--------|-----------|
| pVCF_to_plink | 8 | 32 GB | 2h |
| plink_filter_merge | 16 | 64 GB | 4h |
| gvcf_to_signalintensity | 8 | 64 GB | 4h per batch |
| pfb_partial | 4 | 32 GB | 1h per batch |
| filter_baf_lrr_files | 2 | 4 GB | 1h per batch |

Memory and time limits double automatically on retry (up to 3 attempts).

---

## Reference genome

GRCh38. Problematic genomic regions used for filtering are included in:
```
scripts/resources/Genome_Regions_data_GRCh38.bed
```

